        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Words To Keep Straight",
          "text": "The value is the referent, the act is a borrow, and the window in which the reference must stay valid is its lifetime. A `&String` points at the stack triple, not at the heap bytes."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Shared Means Read-Only",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`&T` grants read access, never mutation through it.",
            "Many `&T` to one value may coexist — aliasing is fine.",
            "No mutation means no reader ever sees a torn value.",
            "Mutating the owner while a `&T` is live is E0502."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "It Copies, It Never Moves"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`&T` is itself `Copy`: assigning duplicates the pointer.",
            "Pass a `&T` to ten functions, still hold it after.",
            "Method calls auto-borrow: `v.len()` is `Vec::len(&v)`.",
            "Never write `&v` by hand for a method receiver."
          ]
        },
