      "page_title": "Shared &T in Practice & Exclusive &mut T",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`&T` for a sized `T` is exactly one machine word.",
            "`&str` and `&[T]` are fat pointers: pointer plus length.",
            "`&&T` appears in closures: `filter(|x: &&i32| **x > 0)`.",
            "Auto-deref hides the double reference in comparisons."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Threads Read For Free",
          "items": [
            "`&T` is `Send` exactly when `T: Sync`.",
            "That is the basis of scoped-thread read sharing.",
            "No lock needed while nobody can write."
          ],
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Why does pushing inside a `&self` method fail?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "`&self` is a shared borrow of the whole struct.",
            "`push` needs exclusive access to the field.",
            "Change the receiver to `&mut self`."
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "fn add(&self, x: i32) { self.items.push(x); } // no",
            "fn add(&mut self, x: i32) { self.items.push(x); }"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Start Here Every Time",
          "text": "Default every parameter to `&T`. Escalate to `&mut T` only when you must write, and to owned `T` only when you must store or consume."
        },
