          "title": "Invariance, Concretely",
          "text": "A `&mut Vec<&'long str>` is not usable as `&mut Vec<&'short str>`. If it were, a caller could push short-lived data into long-lived storage and read it after the data died."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Sequence the borrows so the first dies before the second.",
            "Or split the data with `split_at_mut` for disjoint halves.",
            "Deleting the later use of `a` alone often compiles it."
          ]
        }
      ]
